tion). Two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sequences are canonically equivalent if they are equal when sorting the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scalars in ascending order by their combining class.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For example, consider the sequence ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"\\u{0041}\\u{0301}\\u{0316}\""},{"text":" (LATIN","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"CAPITAL LETTER A, COMBINING ACUTE ACCENT, COMBINING GRAVE ACCENT BELOW).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The combining classes of these scalars have the numeric values 0, 230, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"220, respectively. Sorting these scalars by their combining classes yields","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"\\u{0041}\\u{0316}\\u{0301}\""},{"text":", so two strings that differ only by the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ordering of those scalars would compare as equal:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let aboveBeforeBelow = \"\\u{0041}\\u{0301}\\u{0316}\"","let belowBeforeAbove = \"\\u{0041}\\u{0316}\\u{0301}\"","print(aboveBeforeBelow == belowBeforeAbove)","\/\/ Prints \"true\""]},{"type":"heading","text":"Named and Unnamed Combining Classes","anchor":"Named-and-Unnamed-Combining-Classes","level":1},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Canonical combining classes are defined in the Unicode Standard as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"integers in the range ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...254"},{"text":". For convenience, the standard assigns","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbolic names to a subset of these combining classes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CanonicalCombiningClass"},{"text":" type conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RawRepresentable"},{"text":" with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"raw value of type ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UInt8"},{"text":". You can create instances of the type by using","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the static members named after the symbolic names, or by using the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(rawValue:)"},{"text":" initializer.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let overlayClass = Unicode.CanonicalCombiningClass(rawValue: 1)","let overlayClassIsOverlay = overlayClass == .overlay","\/\/ overlayClassIsOverlay == true"]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Unicode\/CanonicalCombiningClass"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Unicode\/GeneralCategory","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Unicode\/NumericType"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Unicode-Scalar-Classifications","title":"Unicode Scalar Classifications"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"The classification of a scalar used in the Canonical Ordering Algorithm","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"defined by the Unicode Standard."}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Unicode.CanonicalCombiningClass","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CanonicalCombiningClass","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CanonicalCombiningClass","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:s7UnicodeO23CanonicalCombiningClassV","extendedModule":"Swift","platforms":[{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"name":"iOS"},{"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name